{{!--
  WHERE A REQUEST CAME FROM: the rows a security email adds to its detail
  card, between DetailBoxStart and DetailBoxEnd, under the row that says
  when - so its owner can tell their own request from somebody else's.
  Common/Server/Utils/RequestOrigin/RequestOriginUtil.getEmailVars writes
  all three values.

  Each is printed escaped (plainText): the device is built only of names
  UserAgentDevice spells out and the place only of what a header the
  operator named says, but neither is markup. A row without a value does
  not show - an installation that names no geo header has no location, and
  an email with no request behind it has none of the three.
--}}
{{> DetailBoxField title="IP address:" plainText=requestIpAddress }}
{{> DetailBoxField title="Approximate location:" plainText=requestLocation }}
{{> DetailBoxField title="Device:" plainText=requestDevice }}
